design:
PLAN: icon set for the Rebase dialog's options, drawn from `jj rebase --help`'s own vocabulary; theme-aware via the existing icon pipeline.
Options needing glyphs (RebaseDialog radio buttons; ui/rebase/RebaseDialog.kt `destModeOnto/After/Before` :~76-109 and the source-mode radios backed by `RebaseSourceMode` (jj/Revset.kt:226-235: `-r` REVISION "only these revisions; descendants stay", `-s` SOURCE "revision and all descendants", `-b` BRANCH "the entire branch containing the revision") and `RebaseDestinationMode` (`-d` ONTO, `-A` INSERT_AFTER, `-B` INSERT_BEFORE)): 6 glyphs, 16x16, single-colour SVG (`currentColor`-recoloured by `SvgIcon`/`JujutsuIcons` helpers, see JujutsuIcons.kt:51-76) so they follow themes.
Icon concepts (from jj's docs diagrams: `jj rebase --help` shows ASCII before/after pictures for -r/-s/-b and -d/-A/-B): 
 - `-r` revision: a single node lifted out of a chain (one dot with an arrow to a new parent; neighbours reconnect);
 - `-s` source: a node plus its descendant chain moving together (a short vertical chain with an arrow);
 - `-b` branch: a forked branch shape (Y) moving as a whole;
 - `-d` onto: node placed on top of the destination (dot above destination dot, arrow down);
 - `-A` insert after: node inserted below destination in the chain (dot between destination and its child);
 - `-B` insert before: node inserted above destination (dot between destination's parent and destination).
Wire: `JujutsuIcons.RebaseRevision/Source/Branch`, `RebaseOnto/After/Before` loaded from `icons/rebase*.svg` (new files; naming matches existing `rebase.svg`, `squash.svg`); shown on the radio buttons (`JRadioButton.icon` is awkward - radios already render the selection circle; Rec: put the icon in the button's label via `JBLabel(icon, text)` next to the radio or use `JBRadioButton` with `icon` + `iconTextGap` - the platform DSL (`panel { buttonsGroup { radioButton(text).applyToComponent { icon = ... }}}`) supports it); also reuse the same icons in the DnD drop hints and the drag-rebase source-mode picker (`dragRebaseSourceMode` setting UI) so the vocabulary is consistent.
Decisions made without the user: Q: who draws? Rec: I author simple geometric SVGs for your review (like kcgf); Q: icons in dialogs only or also context menu entries (Rebase Onto/After...)? Rec dialog + DnD hints only (menus use the generic rebase icon).
Scale: none. Testing: resource-exists/parse test (all six load; XML well-formed), existing RebaseDialog tests unaffected; visual review light/dark/new UI at 100/200% (headless can't assert pixels, see jj-idea-s01y). Manual: MT-CTXMENU rebase dialog + MT-DND hint rows. Regression scope: MT-CTXMENU, MT-DND.
